{
 "id": "2026-10-10-beyond-hormuz",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Iran's navy now says it will chase ships far beyond the Strait of Hormuz."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "On Friday, Iran's Revolutionary Guard said it hit a gas tanker, the Sunshine. Its navy says the ship tried an unauthorized route south of the strait. The Guard claims a fire disabled the engine room. Shipping sources name a different vessel, so details are unclear."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Then came a warning. The Guard says any ship on such routes will be pursued and punished anywhere in the region. Earlier this week, two vessels were hit within a day, one off Qatar and one in the Gulf of Oman. Nobody claimed those attacks."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Reuters, citing three maritime security sources, counts at least twelve attacks or harassment cases around Hormuz in one week. That is the highest weekly total since the war began on February 28. Euronews says the strait has been effectively closed since."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Follow for the next update."
  }
 ],
